<div class="re-render-probe">
  <strong>Re-render probe</strong> — edit <code>customFeaturesDemo.note</code> in the sidebar and watch this update:
  <em class="probe-value">{{ note }}</em>
</div>

<div class="test-group">
  <h3 class="test-group__label">Filters</h3>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>excerpt</code>
      <span class="tag tag--auto-mirror">auto-mirror</span>
      <span class="tag tag--edit">edit: sampleText</span>
    </div>
    <p class="test-section__desc">Pure function — no imports. Should auto-mirror into the browser bundle without any override.</p>
    <div class="test-section__output">{{ sampleText | excerpt: 60 }}</div>
    <div class="test-section__raw">Input (first 60 chars): <code>sampleText | excerpt: 60</code></div>
  </div>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>length</code>
      <span class="tag tag--auto-mirror">auto-mirror</span>
      <span class="tag tag--edit">edit: sampleText</span>
    </div>
    <p class="test-section__desc">Pure function — no imports. Should auto-mirror.</p>
    <div class="test-section__output">{{ sampleText | length }}</div>
    <div class="test-section__raw">Expression: <code>sampleText | length</code></div>
  </div>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>stamp</code>
      <span class="tag tag--auto-mirror">auto-mirror (closure)</span>
      <span class="tag tag--edit">edit: sampleText</span>
    </div>
    <p class="test-section__desc">Closes over a module-level <code>buildInfo</code> object in <code>.eleventy.js</code>. The plugin bundles the real config and replays it, so the closure survives — this auto-mirrors with no override and the browser output must match the server. If it regressed to <code>fn.toString()</code>, <code>buildInfo</code> would be undefined in the browser and the re-render would break.</p>
    <div class="test-section__output">{{ sampleText | stamp }}</div>
    <div class="test-section__raw">Expression: <code>sampleText | stamp</code> → expect suffix <code>[build-closure-ok]</code></div>
  </div>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>wordCount</code>
      <span class="tag tag--auto-mirror">auto-mirror</span>
      <span class="tag tag--edit">edit: sampleText</span>
    </div>
    <p class="test-section__desc">Imports a local module (<code>site/js/wordCount.js</code>) whose helpers (<code>htmlToPlainText</code>, <code>plainTextMetadata</code>) are pure string ops. Config-replay bundles that module, so it auto-mirrors — no override.</p>
    <div class="test-section__output">{{ sampleText | wordCount }}</div>
    <div class="test-section__raw">Expression: <code>sampleText | wordCount</code></div>
  </div>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>postDate</code>
      <span class="tag tag--auto-mirror">auto-mirror</span>
      <span class="tag tag--edit">edit: sampleDate</span>
    </div>
    <p class="test-section__desc">Uses Luxon's <code>DateTime</code>. Luxon is a plain npm package that bundles for the browser, so it auto-mirrors — no override. The server and browser renders must be identical (locale pinned to <code>en-US</code>).</p>
    <div class="test-section__output">{{ sampleDate | postDate }}</div>
    <div class="test-section__raw">Expression: <code>sampleDate | postDate</code></div>
  </div>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>markdownify</code>
      <span class="tag tag--auto-mirror">auto-mirror</span>
      <span class="tag tag--edit">edit: sampleMarkdown</span>
    </div>
    <p class="test-section__desc">Closes over a module-level <code>markdown-it</code> instance. Both the closure and markdown-it itself survive bundling, so it auto-mirrors — no override. Browser output matches the full markdown-it render, not just inline patterns.</p>
    <div class="test-section__output">{{ sampleMarkdown | markdownify }}</div>
    <div class="test-section__raw">Expression: <code>sampleMarkdown | markdownify</code></div>
  </div>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>fileSize</code>
      <span class="tag tag--override">browser override (required)</span>
      <span class="tag tag--display-only">display only</span>
    </div>
    <p class="test-section__desc">The one genuine override case. Server-side calls <code>fs.statSync</code> to read a file size from disk; <code>node:fs</code> is stubbed in the browser bundle and can't run there, so this <em>requires</em> a browser override (<code>overrides/filesize-filter.mjs</code>). Server shows a byte count; the browser shows the placeholder <code>— (server-only)</code>.</p>
    <div class="test-section__output">{{ "package.json" | fileSize }}</div>
    <div class="test-section__raw">Expression: <code>"package.json" | fileSize</code></div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="test-group">
  <h3 class="test-group__label">Shortcodes</h3>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>{% raw %}{% year %}{% endraw %}</code>
      <span class="tag tag--auto-mirror">auto-mirror</span>
      <span class="tag tag--display-only">display only</span>
    </div>
    <p class="test-section__desc">Pure function, no closure over any import. Should auto-mirror into the browser bundle without any override.</p>
    <div class="test-section__output">Copyright {% year %} CloudCannon</div>
  </div>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>{% raw %}{% isoDate %}{% endraw %}</code>
      <span class="tag tag--auto-mirror">auto-mirror</span>
      <span class="tag tag--display-only">display only</span>
    </div>
    <p class="test-section__desc">Uses Luxon's <code>DateTime.now()</code>. Luxon bundles for the browser, so it auto-mirrors — no override. Output differs between server (build time) and browser (render time), which is expected for a clock value.</p>
    <div class="test-section__output">{% isoDate %}</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="test-group">
  <h3 class="test-group__label">Paired Shortcodes</h3>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>{% raw %}{% callout type %}…{% endcallout %}{% endraw %}</code>
      <span class="tag tag--auto-mirror">auto-mirror</span>
      <span class="tag tag--edit">edit: calloutType</span>
    </div>
    <p class="test-section__desc">Pure function, no closure over any import. Should auto-mirror. Valid values for <code>calloutType</code>: <code>info</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>error</code>.</p>
    {% callout calloutType %}
      This is a <strong>{{ calloutType }}</strong> callout. Its type is driven by the <code>calloutType</code> field — edit it in the sidebar.
    {% endcallout %}
    {% callout "info" %}
      Literal-string argument: <code>{% raw %}{% callout "info" %}{% endraw %}</code>. Type is hardcoded in the template, not user-editable.
    {% endcallout %}
  </div>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>{% raw %}{% prose %}…{% endprose %}{% endraw %}</code>
      <span class="tag tag--auto-mirror">auto-mirror</span>
      <span class="tag tag--edit">edit: sampleMarkdown</span>
    </div>
    <p class="test-section__desc">Closes over the same module-level <code>markdown-it</code> instance as <code>markdownify</code>; both the closure and markdown-it bundle for the browser, so it auto-mirrors — no override. Edit <code>sampleMarkdown</code> and confirm the rendered HTML updates.</p>
    {% prose %}{{ sampleMarkdown }}{% endprose %}
  </div>
</div>

<div class="test-group">
  <h3 class="test-group__label">Custom Tag</h3>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>{% raw %}{% icon name %}{% endraw %}</code>
      <span class="tag tag--auto-mirror">auto-mirror</span>
      <span class="tag tag--edit">edit: iconName</span>
    </div>
    <p class="test-section__desc">Custom Liquid tag registered with <code>addLiquidTag</code>, which is mirrored like any other helper. The factory uses liquidjs's <code>Tokenizer</code>/<code>evalToken</code> (pulled via <code>require</code>; liquidjs bundles for the browser), so the same factory runs server- and browser-side — no override. Renders a <code>&lt;span class="icon icon-{name}"&gt;</code>. Change <code>iconName</code> and confirm the class updates.</p>
    <div class="test-section__output">
      Variable arg (resolves <code>iconName</code>): {% icon iconName %}
    </div>
    <div class="test-section__output">
      Literal arg: {% icon "envelope" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="test-group">
  <h3 class="test-group__label">includeWith tag</h3>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>{% raw %}{% includeWith "template", obj %}{% endraw %}</code>
      <span class="tag tag--builtin">built-in</span>
      <span class="tag tag--edit">edit: dateDisplay</span>
    </div>
    <p class="test-section__desc">
      The sub-partial below is rendered by <code>{% raw %}{% includeWith "ed-regions-date-display", dateDisplay %}{% endraw %}</code>
      <em>inside this component template</em>, so it runs through the browser liquid engine on every re-render.
      Edit <code>customFeaturesDemo.dateDisplay.date</code> or <code>.label</code> in the sidebar and confirm the sub-partial updates.
    </p>
    <div class="test-section__output">
      {% includeWith "ed-regions-date-display", dateDisplay %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="test-group">
  <h3 class="test-group__label">Built-in browser ports — date filters</h3>
  <p class="test-group__note">These are Eleventy's built-in date filters. The browser bundle ships handwritten ports for them — no auto-mirror, no override needed. Edit <code>sampleDate</code> and confirm all four update.</p>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>dateToRfc3339</code> · <code>dateToRfc822</code> · <code>htmlDateString</code> · <code>postDate</code>
      <span class="tag tag--builtin">built-in port</span>
      <span class="tag tag--edit">edit: sampleDate</span>
    </div>
    <dl class="test-section__output">
      <dt>sampleDate | dateToRfc3339</dt><dd>{{ sampleDate | dateToRfc3339 }}</dd>
      <dt>sampleDate | dateToRfc822</dt><dd>{{ sampleDate | dateToRfc822 }}</dd>
      <dt>sampleDate | htmlDateString</dt><dd>{{ sampleDate | htmlDateString }}</dd>
      <dt>sampleDate | postDate (auto-mirror)</dt><dd>{{ sampleDate | postDate }}</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="test-group">
  <h3 class="test-group__label">Built-in browser ports — slug &amp; url filters</h3>
  <p class="test-group__note">Inputs are hardcoded literals — display only. Confirm the outputs match what the 11ty build would produce.</p>

  <div class="test-section">
    <div class="test-section__header">
      <code>slug</code> · <code>slugify</code> · <code>url</code>
      <span class="tag tag--builtin">built-in port</span>
      <span class="tag tag--display-only">display only</span>
    </div>
    <dl class="test-section__output">
      <dt>"Hello World &amp; More" | slug</dt><dd>{{ "Hello World & More" | slug }}</dd>
      <dt>"Hello World &amp; More" | slugify</dt><dd>{{ "Hello World & More" | slugify }}</dd>
      <dt>"/some/path/" | url</dt><dd>{{ "/some/path/" | url }}</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</div>
